          <item>
           <widget class="QWidget" name="methods_widget" native="true">
            <property name="visible">
             <bool>false</bool>
            </property>
            <layout class="QVBoxLayout" name="methods_layout">
             <property name="spacing">
              <number>10</number>
             </property>
             <property name="leftMargin">
              <number>0</number>
             </property>
             <property name="topMargin">
              <number>6</number>
             </property>
             <property name="rightMargin">
              <number>0</number>
             </property>
             <property name="bottomMargin">
              <number>0</number>
             </property>
             <item>
              <widget class="QLabel" name="methods_label">
               <property name="text">
                <string>&lt;b&gt;Standard spectrum (Welch [1]):&lt;/b&gt; the signal is divided into short windows, a Fast Fourier Transform (FFT) is applied to each window and the periodograms are averaged. The frequency bin resolution is 1 / window length (s): 0.2 Hz with 5 s windows. The power of a few bins is averaged to estimate the power in a frequency band, up to half the sampling rate.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;b&gt;Periodic and aperiodic decomposition:&lt;/b&gt; IRASA [2] and FOOOF [3] separate the oscillatory (periodic) and the fractal (aperiodic) components of the spectrum. They are described in the documentation of the tool (Read more! below).</string>
               </property>
               <property name="textFormat">
                <enum>Qt::TextFormat::RichText</enum>
               </property>
               <property name="wordWrap">
                <bool>true</bool>
               </property>
               <property name="variant" stdset="0">
                <string notr="true">help</string>
               </property>
              </widget>
             </item>
             <item>
              <layout class="QVBoxLayout" name="references_layout">
               <property name="spacing">
                <number>8</number>
               </property>
               <property name="leftMargin">
                <number>0</number>
               </property>
               <property name="topMargin">
                <number>6</number>
               </property>
               <property name="rightMargin">
                <number>0</number>
               </property>
               <property name="bottomMargin">
                <number>0</number>
               </property>
               <item>
                <widget class="QFrame" name="references_line">
                 <property name="frameShape">
                  <enum>QFrame::Shape::HLine</enum>
                 </property>
                 <property name="frameShadow">
                  <enum>QFrame::Shadow::Plain</enum>
                 </property>
                </widget>
               </item>
               <item>
                <widget class="QLabel" name="references_label">
                 <property name="font">
                  <font>
                   <pointsize>10</pointsize>
                  </font>
                 </property>
                 <property name="text">
                  <string>[1] Welch, P. D. (1967). The use of fast Fourier transform for the estimation of power spectra: A method based on time averaging over short, modified periodograms. &lt;i&gt;IEEE Transactions on Audio and Electroacoustics&lt;/i&gt;, &lt;i&gt;15&lt;/i&gt;(2), 70–73. &lt;a href="https://doi.org/10.1109/TAU.1967.1161901"&gt;https://doi.org/10.1109/TAU.1967.1161901&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br/&gt;[2] Wen, H., &amp;amp; Liu, Z. (2016). Separating fractal and oscillatory components in the power spectrum of neurophysiological signal. &lt;i&gt;Brain Topography&lt;/i&gt;, &lt;i&gt;29&lt;/i&gt;(1), 13–26. &lt;a href="https://doi.org/10.1007/s10548-015-0448-0"&gt;https://doi.org/10.1007/s10548-015-0448-0&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br/&gt;[3] Donoghue, T., Haller, M., Peterson, E. J., Varma, P., Sebastian, P., Gao, R., Noto, T., Lara, A. H., Wallis, J. D., Knight, R. T., Shestyuk, A., &amp;amp; Voytek, B. (2020). Parameterizing neural power spectra into periodic and aperiodic components. &lt;i&gt;Nature Neuroscience&lt;/i&gt;, &lt;i&gt;23&lt;/i&gt;(12), 1655–1665. &lt;a href="https://doi.org/10.1038/s41593-020-00744-x"&gt;https://doi.org/10.1038/s41593-020-00744-x&lt;/a&gt;</string>
                 </property>
                 <property name="textFormat">
                  <enum>Qt::TextFormat::RichText</enum>
                 </property>
                 <property name="wordWrap">
                  <bool>true</bool>
                 </property>
                 <property name="openExternalLinks">
                  <bool>true</bool>
                 </property>
                 <property name="variant" stdset="0">
                  <string notr="true">help</string>
                 </property>
                </widget>
               </item>
              </layout>
             </item>
            </layout>
